TITLE:: VSTPluginBrowser
summary:: a VST plugin browser dialog
categories:: GUI
related:: Classes/VSTPlugin, Classes/VSTPluginController, Classes/VSTPluginDesc, Classes/VSTPluginGui

DESCRIPTION::
This class creates a dialog window where you can browse already loaded plugins, start a new search in the default directories
(see link::Classes/VSTPlugin#*search::) or load a plugin from a file dialog.

IMAGE::browser.jpg::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new

ARGUMENT:: model
the link::Classes/VSTPluginController:: instance that should open the plugin.

DISCUSSION::
Typically, you do not create a VSTPluginBrowser yourself. Instead, it is created automatically when you call link::Classes/VSTPluginController#-browse:: or when you press the "Browse" button in link::Classes/VSTPluginGui::.

However, if you create the instance manually, you have more control over the appearance because you have direct access to all the link::Classes/Window:: methods:

code::
// ~vst is the VSTPluginController
b = VSTPluginBrowser(~vst);
// do not destroy on close
b.view.deleteOnClose = false;
// show
b.front;
// close programmatically
b.close;
// show again
b.front;
::

INSTANCEMETHODS::

PRIVATE:: init, prSearchDir, prApplyFilter, prBuildGui, prUpdatePlugins, prSearchRunning, prPluginSelected, prSearch, prOpenFile, prClear, prOpenPlugin
